    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus its base).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: assign `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is purely **derived** from two fields already on `Owner` (`customerCode`, set by `OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice`, and `registrationDate`, defaulted by `OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`), I added it as a computed response field alongside the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`) rather than as a stored column. This keeps structural impact minimal \u2014 no new aspect, no changes to the large `Owner` model class, and no DB-schema edits across the four database dialects.\n\nTwo files touched:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this at build time).\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null\n       ? null\n       : owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n\nThe null guard matters: seed owners have no `customerCode`/`registrationDate`, so an unguarded expression would NPE when those owners are serialized.",
